TITLE: foodcode-pineapple
FCM: NON-DROP FRAME

001  AX       V     C        00:00:00:00 00:00:05:13 00:00:00:00 00:00:05:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE ENZYME
* VISUAL: A whole pineapple with a jagged enzyme shape floating above it, molecular dots drifting
* NARRATION: Scientists have known for decades that fresh pineapple contains an enzyme that digests protein.

002  AX       V     C        00:00:05:13 00:00:10:02 00:00:05:13 00:00:10:02
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT ACID
* VISUAL: A chili and a lemon both crossed out beside a pineapple, red X marks
* NARRATION: Not a spice. Not an acid. An actual digestive enzyme working on you.

003  AX       V     C        00:00:10:02 00:00:14:51 00:00:10:02 00:00:14:51
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU ARE PROTEIN
* VISUAL: A mouth diagram with tongue and cheeks highlighted in bold protein dots
* NARRATION: Your tongue, your cheeks, the inside of your mouth are made of protein.

004  AX       V     C        00:00:14:51 00:00:19:40 00:00:14:51 00:00:19:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: BREAKING YOU DOWN
* VISUAL: An enzyme shape snipping tiny links off a pink tongue surface
* NARRATION: So when you eat pineapple, that enzyme starts breaking down your own tissue.

005  AX       V     C        00:00:19:40 00:00:25:13 00:00:19:40 00:00:25:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT WHAT YOU THINK
* VISUAL: A tongue with spark marks and a big X over a lemon acid bottle
* NARRATION: Stay until the end, because I will show you why that tingle is not acidity.

006  AX       V     C        00:00:25:13 00:00:30:23 00:00:25:13 00:00:30:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE CANNED LIE
* VISUAL: A sad canned pineapple ring, its glowing core gone, empty middle
* NARRATION: And why canned pineapple has been quietly stripped of the one thing that matters.

007  AX       V     C        00:00:30:23 00:00:34:51 00:00:30:23 00:00:34:51
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT A SNACK
* VISUAL: A pineapple cocktail with umbrella crossed out, an enzyme shape beside it
* NARRATION: This is not about a tropical snack. This is about an enzyme.

008  AX       V     C        00:00:34:51 00:00:40:02 00:00:34:51 00:00:40:02
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN YOUR KITCHEN
* VISUAL: A fruit bowl with a pineapple glowing menacingly at the front
* NARRATION: An enzyme that can digest living tissue, and it is inside your fruit bowl.

009  AX       V     C        00:00:40:02 00:00:44:50 00:00:40:02 00:00:44:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: LAST TIME
* VISUAL: A hand holding a fresh pineapple slice outdoors, picnic blanket behind
* NARRATION: Think about the last time you ate fresh pineapple at a summer picnic.

010  AX       V     C        00:00:44:50 00:00:49:16 00:00:44:50 00:00:49:16
* FROM CLIP NAME: SWEET AND JUICY
* VISUAL: A pineapple slice dripping juice with sun rays and a satisfied face
* NARRATION: Sweet, juicy, cold, and exactly what you wanted on a hot afternoon.

011  AX       V     C        00:00:49:16 00:00:52:52 00:00:49:16 00:00:52:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: ONE MINUTE IN
* VISUAL: A clock at one minute beside an open mouth with question marks
* NARRATION: Then about a minute in, the edges of your tongue start to feel strange.

012  AX       V     C        00:00:52:52 00:00:55:58 00:00:52:52 00:00:55:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE TINGLE
* VISUAL: A tongue covered in tiny sparks with a rough sandpaper texture patch
* NARRATION: A tingle. A slight burn. Your tongue feels raw, almost like sandpaper.

013  AX       V     C        00:00:55:58 00:00:59:18 00:00:55:58 00:00:59:18
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU BLAMED ACID
* VISUAL: A lemon squeezing onto a tongue with an arrow labelled acid
* NARRATION: You probably assumed it was the acid in the fruit attacking your mouth.

014  AX       V     C        00:00:59:18 00:01:02:23 00:00:59:18 00:01:02:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: OR AN ALLERGY
* VISUAL: A person scratching their arm with an allergy warning sign above
* NARRATION: Maybe you even wondered whether you were secretly mildly allergic to pineapple.

015  AX       V     C        00:01:02:23 00:01:05:44 00:01:02:23 00:01:05:44
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOBODY TOLD YOU
* VISUAL: A fruit stand with a hidden curtain and a secret glowing behind it
* NARRATION: But here is what nobody told you at that fruit stand that morning.

016  AX       V     C        00:01:05:44 00:01:09:04 00:01:05:44 00:01:09:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: BROMELAIN
* VISUAL: A bromelain enzyme shape cutting into a tongue with tiny scissors
* NARRATION: That sensation is not acidity. It is an enzyme called bromelain digesting you.

017  AX       V     C        00:01:09:04 00:01:12:25 00:01:09:04 00:01:12:25
* FROM CLIP NAME: EATING YOU BACK
* VISUAL: A pineapple with a wide mouth chewing on a tiny running person
* NARRATION: Fresh pineapple is not burning your mouth. It is chemically eating you back.

018  AX       V     C        00:01:12:25 00:01:15:30 00:01:12:25 00:01:15:30
* FROM CLIP NAME: PROTEASES
* VISUAL: A row of little enzyme characters standing in a family photo line
* NARRATION: Bromelain is not one enzyme. It is a whole family of proteases.

019  AX       V     C        00:01:15:30 00:01:18:50 00:01:15:30 00:01:18:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: CUTTING PROTEIN
* VISUAL: Scissor-shaped enzymes snipping a long chain of coloured protein beads
* NARRATION: Proteases cut protein chains apart, exactly like the enzymes in your stomach do.

020  AX       V     C        00:01:18:50 00:01:22:11 00:01:18:50 00:01:22:11
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE CORE
* VISUAL: A pineapple cross-section with the tough core glowing bright yellow
* NARRATION: And in pineapple, this family is concentrated in the stem and the core.

021  AX       V     C        00:01:22:11 00:01:25:31 00:01:22:11 00:01:25:31
* FROM CLIP NAME: THROWN AWAY
* VISUAL: A hand dropping a pineapple core into a trash can
* NARRATION: The fibrous core most people cut away and throw straight into the bin.

022  AX       V     C        00:01:25:31 00:01:29:07 00:01:25:31 00:01:29:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE JELL-O PROBLEM
* VISUAL: A kitchen counter with a wobbly bowl of unset jelly and a spoon
* NARRATION: There is a famous kitchen proof of this, and you have probably seen it.

023  AX       V     C        00:01:29:07 00:01:32:59 00:01:29:07 00:01:32:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: IT NEVER SETS
* VISUAL: A bowl of liquid jelly with pineapple chunks, an hourglass beside it
* NARRATION: Fresh pineapple in jelly means the jelly never sets, no matter how long you wait.

024  AX       V     C        00:01:32:59 00:01:36:19 00:01:32:59 00:01:36:19
* FROM CLIP NAME: COLLAGEN
* VISUAL: A wobbling gelatin cube labelled collagen, an enzyme taking a bite
* NARRATION: Gelatin is made of collagen, and collagen is a protein. Bromelain eats protein.

025  AX       V     C        00:01:36:19 00:01:39:40 00:01:36:19 00:01:39:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: CHEWED THROUGH
* VISUAL: Enzymes chewing through a jelly cube that keeps collapsing into liquid
* NARRATION: So the enzyme chews through the jelly faster than it can ever set.

026  AX       V     C        00:01:39:40 00:01:42:45 00:01:39:40 00:01:42:45
* FROM CLIP NAME: CANNED WORKS
* VISUAL: A can of pineapple rings beside a perfectly set firm jelly bowl
* NARRATION: Canned pineapple works perfectly in jelly, and there is one reason only.

027  AX       V     C        00:01:42:45 00:01:45:50 00:01:42:45 00:01:45:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: HEAT DESTROYS IT
* VISUAL: A pineapple can in a factory with heat waves and a thermometer at sixty
* NARRATION: Canning heats the fruit past sixty degrees, and that destroys bromelain permanently.

028  AX       V     C        00:01:45:50 00:01:48:56 00:01:45:50 00:01:48:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: HEAT KILLS IT
* VISUAL: A grilled pineapple slice with a dead flat enzyme shape beside it
* NARRATION: Heat kills the enzyme. That is also why cooked pineapple never tingles.

029  AX       V     C        00:01:48:56 00:01:53:02 00:01:48:56 00:01:53:02
* FROM CLIP NAME: GONE
* VISUAL: Pineapple on a grill with the enzyme vanishing upward in steam
* NARRATION: Roast it, grill it, bake it, and the enzyme is gone before it reaches your plate.

030  AX       V     C        00:01:53:02 00:01:56:54 00:01:53:02 00:01:56:54
* FROM CLIP NAME: IT GOES DEEPER
* VISUAL: An enzyme walking past a mouth signpost heading down a tunnel
* NARRATION: Here is where the story genuinely turns. The enzyme does not stop at your mouth.

031  AX       V     C        00:01:56:54 00:02:00:30 00:01:56:54 00:02:00:30
* FROM CLIP NAME: SURVIVES THE STOMACH
* VISUAL: An enzyme swimming through a bubbling acid pool, unharmed and smiling
* NARRATION: Bromelain is one of the very few food enzymes that survives your stomach acid.

032  AX       V     C        00:02:00:30 00:02:03:50 00:02:00:30 00:02:03:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: INTO THE BLOOD
* VISUAL: An enzyme passing through an intestine wall into a red bloodstream river
* NARRATION: It reaches your small intestine intact, and from there it enters your bloodstream.

033  AX       V     C        00:02:03:50 00:02:06:56 00:02:03:50 00:02:06:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: THREE THINGS
* VISUAL: A clipboard with three numbered boxes, the enzyme standing beside it
* NARRATION: Once it is circulating in your body, it does three measurable things.

034  AX       V     C        00:02:06:56 00:02:10:01 00:02:06:56 00:02:10:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: FIBRIN
* VISUAL: A net of fibrin around a wound being snipped apart by enzymes
* NARRATION: It breaks down fibrin, the protein mesh that forms around injured tissue.

035  AX       V     C        00:02:10:01 00:02:13:07 00:02:10:01 00:02:13:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: PAIN SIGNALS
* VISUAL: Pain signal molecules blocked by stop signs held up by enzymes
* NARRATION: It suppresses the signalling molecules that drive pain and swelling after injury.

036  AX       V     C        00:02:13:07 00:02:16:27 00:02:13:07 00:02:16:27
* FROM CLIP NAME: THINS MUCUS
* VISUAL: Thick gloopy mucus turning thin and watery with a happy sinus diagram
* NARRATION: And it thins mucus, which is why it shows up in sinus treatments.

037  AX       V     C        00:02:16:27 00:02:19:32 00:02:16:27 00:02:19:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: GERMAN SURGEONS
* VISUAL: A surgeon in scrubs handing a bromelain capsule to a bandaged patient
* NARRATION: German surgeons have given bromelain to patients after operations to reduce swelling.

038  AX       V     C        00:02:19:32 00:02:22:38 00:02:19:32 00:02:22:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: SINUS TREATMENT
* VISUAL: A map of Europe with a calm sinus diagram glowing over it
* NARRATION: It is a recognised treatment for sinus inflammation across several European countries.

039  AX       V     C        00:02:22:38 00:02:25:43 00:02:22:38 00:02:25:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: JOINT PAIN
* VISUAL: A knee joint diagram with pain stars fading away one by one
* NARRATION: Clinical trials have measured it reducing joint pain in people with osteoarthritis.

040  AX       V     C        00:02:25:43 00:02:28:49 00:02:25:43 00:02:28:49
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN HUMANS
* VISUAL: A petri dish and a mouse both crossed out, a human figure highlighted
* NARRATION: Not in a petri dish. Not in mice. In actual human beings.

041  AX       V     C        00:02:28:49 00:02:32:25 00:02:28:49 00:02:32:25
* FROM CLIP NAME: SHOCKED RESEARCHERS
* VISUAL: A researcher with wide eyes, clipboard shaking, magnifying glass on enzyme
* NARRATION: But the part that shocked even the researchers is how selective this enzyme is.

042  AX       V     C        00:02:32:25 00:02:35:30 00:02:32:25 00:02:35:30
* FROM CLIP NAME: BLUNT TOOL
* VISUAL: A giant hammer squashing a whole army of immune cells flat
* NARRATION: Most anti-inflammatory drugs blunt your entire immune system, like a heavy hammer.

043  AX       V     C        00:02:35:30 00:02:38:50 00:02:35:30 00:02:38:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: SMARTER
* VISUAL: An enzyme holding a fine laser scalpel, precision glowing at the tip
* NARRATION: Bromelain does something smarter. It works like a scalpel instead of a hammer.

044  AX       V     C        00:02:38:50 00:02:41:56 00:02:38:50 00:02:41:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: SELECTIVE
* VISUAL: Only the red swelling signal being snipped while green signals float past
* NARRATION: It selectively reduces the signalling molecules that cause swelling, and nothing else.

045  AX       V     C        00:02:41:56 00:02:45:01 00:02:41:56 00:02:45:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: LEFT ALONE
* VISUAL: Healthy immune cells standing in formation, untouched and saluting
* NARRATION: The rest of your immune response keeps working exactly as it should.

046  AX       V     C        00:02:45:01 00:02:48:22 00:02:45:01 00:02:48:22
* FROM CLIP NAME: NO DRUG DOES THIS
* VISUAL: A medicine bottle shrugging beside a fresh pineapple with a trophy
* NARRATION: No approved drug works through this pathway, at this dose, from this food.

047  AX       V     C        00:02:48:22 00:02:51:27 00:02:48:22 00:02:51:27
* FROM CLIP NAME: THREE STEPS
* VISUAL: A bold title card with three steps written in hand-drawn capitals
* NARRATION: So what do you actually do with this? Three steps. Simple. Specific.

048  AX       V     C        00:02:51:27 00:02:54:32 00:02:51:27 00:02:54:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP ONE: FRESH
* VISUAL: A fresh pineapple with a tick beside a can with a cross
* NARRATION: Step one: eat fresh pineapple, never canned, because canning destroys the enzyme.

049  AX       V     C        00:02:54:32 00:02:57:38 00:02:54:32 00:02:57:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP TWO: NEVER COOK
* VISUAL: A thermometer at sixty degrees with a flame and a dead enzyme
* NARRATION: Step two: never cook it. Heat above sixty degrees kills bromelain permanently.

050  AX       V     C        00:02:57:38 00:03:01:14 00:02:57:38 00:03:01:14
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP THREE: EAT THE CORE
* VISUAL: A pineapple core glowing with a concentration bar chart at maximum
* NARRATION: Step three: eat the core, because that is where the protease concentration is highest.

051  AX       V     C        00:03:01:14 00:03:04:34 00:03:01:14 00:03:04:34
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOBODY SAYS IT
* VISUAL: A tall stack of research papers with a tiny megaphone beside them
* NARRATION: This is all in the scientific literature, but almost nobody communicates it properly.

052  AX       V     C        00:03:04:34 00:03:08:41 00:03:04:34 00:03:08:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE MISSION
* VISUAL: A bridge being built between a laboratory and a home kitchen counter
* NARRATION: That gap between the research and your kitchen is exactly what Food Code exists to close.

053  AX       V     C        00:03:08:41 00:03:12:01 00:03:08:41 00:03:12:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU CHANGED
* VISUAL: A person transformed, glowing brain, looking thoughtfully at a pineapple
* NARRATION: After today, you are no longer someone who eats pineapple without thinking twice.

054  AX       V     C        00:03:12:01 00:03:15:07 00:03:12:01 00:03:15:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU UNDERSTAND
* VISUAL: A brain with a bromelain label connecting dots to a tingling tongue
* NARRATION: You understand what bromelain does to protein, and why your tongue tingles.

055  AX       V     C        00:03:15:07 00:03:18:27 00:03:15:07 00:03:18:27
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU KNOW WHY
* VISUAL: A dead flat enzyme in a can beside a flame, both labelled dead
* NARRATION: You know why the canned stuff is dead, and why heat destroys everything.

056  AX       V     C        00:03:18:27 00:03:21:32 00:03:18:27 00:03:21:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: EVERY DECISION
* VISUAL: A supermarket produce aisle with a glowing arrow to the fresh pineapples
* NARRATION: That knowledge changes every single decision you make in the produce aisle.

057  AX       V     C        00:03:21:32 00:03:25:08 00:03:21:32 00:03:25:08
* FROM CLIP NAME: TELL ME
* VISUAL: A speech bubble comment box with a tingling tongue emoji inside
* NARRATION: Tell me in the comments, have you ever felt that tingle on your tongue?

058  AX       V     C        00:03:25:08 00:03:28:29 00:03:25:08 00:03:28:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: I READ THEM
* VISUAL: A stack of comment cards, one with a reply badge, a pen ready
* NARRATION: I read every single one of them, and I answer the good ones.

059  AX       V     C        00:03:28:29 00:03:32:35 00:03:28:29 00:03:32:35
* FROM CLIP NAME: NEXT: GINGER
* VISUAL: A ginger root with a spotlight, a stomach diagram waiting beside it
* NARRATION: In the next video, I am going to show you what ginger does to your stomach.

060  AX       V     C        00:03:32:35 00:03:36:11 00:03:32:35 00:03:36:11
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOUR STOMACH
* VISUAL: Immune system and cells crossed out, stomach circled with a warning star
* NARRATION: Not your immune system, not your cells, your stomach. And it is not nothing.

